notes:    Built with -DNOCURL so only zlib is required; bwWrite.c is
          compiled but unused at runtime (write APIs not exposed by vv).

local patches (re-apply after any re-vendor; grep "LOCAL PATCH (vv)"):
  bwValues.c  fix a misaligned load in the interval decoder (UB on aarch64,
              found by the ASan/UBSan CI job).
  bwRead.c    readChromLeaf(): bounds-check the chromId against cl->nKeys
              before using it as a subscript. Upstream writes cl->len[idx]
              and cl->chrom[idx] with idx taken verbatim from the file while
              both arrays are calloc'd to the file's own itemCount, so a
              crafted chromosome B-tree corrupts the heap at open. Also frees
              a duplicated chromId's earlier bwStrdup() instead of leaking it.
              Not reported upstream yet; present in 0.4.8.

          Update by re-running:
            git clone --depth 1 --branch <tag> https://github.com/dpryan79/libBigWig
          then re-apply the patches above and re-run the suite.
